          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the mop that matches your floors and your patience. If you mop large tile or vinyl floors, have pets or kids, and want the cleanest result with the least thought, the O-Cedar EasyWring RinseClean is worth its premium because it keeps dirty water out of the job. If you will change the water halfway, the standard EasyWring does the same wringing for less, and the Libman Tornado is the pick if foot pedals are not for you.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your floors are mostly sealed hardwood or laminate, skip the bucket. A Bona Premium Spray Mop, a wide Turbo flat mop or a refillable Rubbermaid Reveal puts down a light mist instead of a wet head, which is what those floors need. Whatever you choose, vacuum first, use less cleaner than you think, wash microfiber without softener, and replace heads before they start smearing.
